# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Panimula {#1-introduction}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bits, gates, and circuits are the basic building blocks of quantum computing. You will learn quantum computation with the circuit model using quantum bits and gates, and also review the superposition, measurement, and entanglement.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga bit, gate, at circuit ang pangunahing pundasyon ng quantum computing. Matututunan mo ang quantum computation gamit ang circuit model na gumagamit ng mga quantum bit at gate, at susuriin din natin ang superposition, measurement, at entanglement.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson you will learn:\n"
"- Single-qubit gates\n"
"- Bloch sphere\n"
"- Superposition\n"
"- Measurement\n"
"- Two-qubit gates and entanglement state\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa araling ito, matututunan mo ang:\n"
"- Mga single-qubit gate\n"
"- Bloch sphere\n"
"- Superposition\n"
"- Measurement\n"
"- Mga two-qubit gate at entanglement state\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the end of this lecture, you will learn about circuit depth, which is essential for utility-scale quantum computing.\n"
msgstr "Sa katapusan ng lekturang ito, matututunan mo ang tungkol sa circuit depth, na napakahalaga para sa utility-scale quantum computing.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Computation as a diagram {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"
msgstr "2. Computation bilang isang diagram {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using qubits or bits, we need to manipulate them in order to turn the inputs we have into the outputs we need. For the simplest programs with very few bits, it is useful to represent this process in a diagram known as a *circuit diagram*.\n"
msgstr "Kapag gumagamit ng mga qubit o bit, kailangan nating manipulahin ang mga ito para ma-convert ang mga input na mayroon tayo sa mga output na kailangan natin. Para sa mga pinakasimpleng programa na may kakaunting bit, kapaki-pakinabang na ipakita ang prosesong ito sa pamamagitan ng isang diagram na tinatawag na *circuit diagram*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bottom-left figure is an example of a classical circuit, and the bottom-right figure is an example of a quantum circuit. In both cases, the inputs are on the left and the outputs are on the right, while the operations are represented by symbols. The symbols used for the operations are called “gates”, mostly for historical reasons.\n"
msgstr "Ang figure sa ibabang-kaliwa ay isang halimbawa ng classical circuit, at ang figure sa ibabang-kanan ay isang halimbawa ng quantum circuit. Sa parehong kaso, ang mga input ay nasa kaliwa at ang mga output ay nasa kanan, habang ang mga operasyon ay kinakatawan ng mga simbolo. Ang mga simbolong ginagamit para sa mga operasyon ay tinatawag na \"mga gate\", kadalasan sa makasaysayang dahilan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"
msgstr "![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"

