# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit uses **Little Endian** notation when ordering qubits and bits, meaning **qubit 0 is the rightmost bit** in the bitstrings. Example: $|01\\rangle$ means q0 is $|1\\rangle$ and q1 is $|0\\rangle$. Be careful because some literature in quantum computing use the Big Endian notation (qubit 0 is the leftmost bit) and a great deal of quantum mechanics literature does, too.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang Qiskit ng **Little Endian** na notasyon sa pag-aayos ng mga qubit at bit, ibig sabihin ang **qubit 0 ay ang pinakakanang bit** sa mga bitstring. Halimbawa: ang $|01\\rangle$ ay nangangahulugang ang q0 ay $|1\\rangle$ at ang q1 ay $|0\\rangle$. Mag-ingat dahil ang ilang literatura sa quantum computing ay gumagamit ng Big Endian na notasyon (ang qubit 0 ay ang pinakakaliwang bit), at ganoon din ang maraming literatura sa quantum mechanics.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another thing to notice is that when representing a quantum circuit, $|q_0\\rangle$ is always placed at the top of the circuit.\n"
"With this in mind, the quantum state of the above circuit can be written as a tensor product of single-qubit quantum state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isa pang bagay na dapat mapansin — kapag kinakatawan ang isang quantum circuit, ang $|q_0\\rangle$ ay laging nasa itaas ng circuit.\n"
"Dahil dito, ang quantum state ng circuit sa itaas ay maisusulat bilang tensor product ng mga single-qubit quantum state.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\n"
"|q1\\rangle \\otimes|q0\\rangle = (a|0\\rangle+b|1\\rangle) \\otimes (c|0\\rangle+d|1\\rangle)\n"
"$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\n"
"|q1\\rangle \\otimes|q0\\rangle = (a|0\\rangle+b|1\\rangle) \\otimes (c|0\\rangle+d|1\\rangle)\n"
"$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\n"
"= ac|0\\rangle|0\\rangle+ad|0\\rangle|1\\rangle+bc|1\\rangle|0\\rangle+bd|1\\rangle|1\\rangle\n"
"$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\n"
"= ac|0\\rangle|0\\rangle+ad|0\\rangle|1\\rangle+bc|1\\rangle|0\\rangle+bd|1\\rangle|1\\rangle\n"
"$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\n"
"= ac|00\\rangle+ad|01\\rangle+bc|10\\rangle+bd|11\\rangle\n"
"$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\n"
"= ac|00\\rangle+ad|01\\rangle+bc|10\\rangle+bd|11\\rangle\n"
"$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "( $|ac|^2+ |ad|^2+ |bc|^2+ |bd|^2=1$ )\n"
msgstr "( $|ac|^2+ |ad|^2+ |bc|^2+ |bd|^2=1$ )\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The initial state of Qiskit is $|0\\rangle|0\\rangle=|00\\rangle$, so by applying $H$ to each qubit, it changes to a state of equal superposition.\n"
msgstr "Ang initial state ng Qiskit ay $|0\\rangle|0\\rangle=|00\\rangle$, kaya sa pag-apply ng $H$ sa bawat qubit, nagbabago ito sa isang estado ng pantay na superposition.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$H|0\\rangle \\otimes H|0\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2}(|00\\rangle+|01\\rangle+|10\\rangle+|11\\rangle)$\n"
msgstr "$H|0\\rangle \\otimes H|0\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2}(|00\\rangle+|01\\rangle+|10\\rangle+|11\\rangle)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{1}{2}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\otimes \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{1}{2}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\otimes \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The measurement rule is also same as a single qubit case, the probability of measuring $|00\\rangle$ is $|ac|^2$.\n"
msgstr "Ang panuntuan sa pagsukat ay katulad din ng sa single qubit — ang posibilidad na masukat ang $|00\\rangle$ ay $|ac|^2$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/ebdf591f-18d0-4fd1-a3a3-b1cdac13bd97-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/ebdf591f-18d0-4fd1-a3a3-b1cdac13bd97-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's measure this circuit.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, sukatin natin ang circuit na ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/2afdd5ac-e51a-4d94-9307-955cc8fbf821-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/2afdd5ac-e51a-4d94-9307-955cc8fbf821-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, we will use a Aer simulator, again, to experimentally verify that the relative probabilities of all possible output states are roughly equal.\n"
msgstr "Gagamitin natin muli ang Aer simulator para eksperimentong mapatunayan na ang relatibong posibilidad ng lahat ng posibleng output state ay halos pantay-pantay.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/060512ac-a106-4ecd-94f5-119048a08467-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/060512ac-a106-4ecd-94f5-119048a08467-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As expected, the states $|00\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|11\\rangle$ were measured almost 25% each.\n"
msgstr "Gaya ng inaasahan, ang mga estado na $|00\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|11\\rangle$ ay nasukat na halos 25% bawat isa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.2 Multi-qubit quantum gates {#42-multi-qubit-quantum-gates}"
msgstr "4.2 Multi-qubit quantum gates {#42-multi-qubit-quantum-gates}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "CNOT gate {#cnot-gate}"
msgstr "CNOT gate {#cnot-gate}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A CNOT(\"controlled NOT\" or CX) gate is a two-qubit gate, meaning its action involves two qubits at once: the control qubit and the target qubit. A CNOT flips the target qubit only when the control qubit is $|1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Ang CNOT (\"controlled NOT\" o CX) gate ay isang two-qubit gate — ang kilos nito ay kinabibilangan ng dalawang qubit nang sabay-sabay: ang control qubit at ang target qubit. Bina-flip ng CNOT ang target qubit tanging kapag ang control qubit ay nasa $|1\\rangle$ na estado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Input (target,control) | Output (target,control) |\n"
"|:-----------:|:------------:|\n"
"| 00          | 00           |\n"
"| 01          | 11           |\n"
"| 10          | 10           |\n"
"| 11          | 01           |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Input (target, control) | Output (target, control) |\n"
"|:-----------:|:------------:|\n"
"| 00          | 00           |\n"
"| 01          | 11           |\n"
"| 10          | 10           |\n"
"| 11          | 01           |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us first simulate the action of this two-qubit gate when q0 and q1 are both $|0\\rangle$, and obtain the output statevector. The Qiskit syntax used is ```qc.cx(control qubit, target qubit)```.\n"
msgstr "Una, i-simulate natin ang kilos ng two-qubit gate na ito kapag ang q0 at q1 ay parehong nasa $|0\\rangle$, at kunin ang output statevector. Ang Qiskit syntax na ginagamit ay ```qc.cx(control qubit, target qubit)```.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/a5621efd-dd9f-4ea4-bf3a-be3cacb45287-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/a5621efd-dd9f-4ea4-bf3a-be3cacb45287-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As expected, applying a CNOT gate on $|00\\rangle$ did not change the state, since the control qubit was in the $|0\\rangle$ state.\n"
"Let's get back to our CNOT operation. This time we will apply a CNOT gate to $|01\\rangle$ and see what happens.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng inaasahan, ang pag-apply ng CNOT gate sa $|00\\rangle$ ay hindi nagbago ng estado, dahil ang control qubit ay nasa $|0\\rangle$ na estado.\n"
"Bumalik tayo sa ating CNOT operation. Sa pagkakataong ito, mag-a-apply tayo ng CNOT gate sa $|01\\rangle$ at titingnan kung ano ang mangyayari.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/5a02de82-44ff-40eb-b64c-2389d6eae3ee-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/5a02de82-44ff-40eb-b64c-2389d6eae3ee-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By applying a CNOT gate, the $|01\\rangle$ state has now become $|11\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Sa pag-apply ng CNOT gate, ang estado na $|01\\rangle$ ay naging $|11\\rangle$ na.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us verify these results by running the circuit on a simulator.\n"
msgstr "I-verify natin ang mga resultang ito sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng circuit sa isang simulator.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/abcafb77-20bf-4bb7-bf8d-57f33af280c1-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/abcafb77-20bf-4bb7-bf8d-57f33af280c1-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/88b76f1d-083b-4f28-b415-380738d22599-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/88b76f1d-083b-4f28-b415-380738d22599-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The results should show you that $|11\\rangle$ has been measured with 100% probability.\n"
msgstr "Dapat ipakita ng mga resulta na ang $|11\\rangle$ ay nasukat nang may 100% na posibilidad.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.3 Quantum entanglement and execution on a real quantum device {#43-quantum-entanglement-and-execution-on-a-real-quantum-device}"
msgstr "4.3 Quantum entanglement at pagpapatakbo sa tunay na quantum device {#43-quantum-entanglement-and-execution-on-a-real-quantum-device}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's start by introducing a specific entangled state which is particularly important in quantum computation, then we'll define the term \"entangled\":\n"
msgstr "Magsimula tayo sa pagpapakilala ng isang partikular na entangled state na napakahalagang sa quantum computation, saka natin bibigyang-kahulugan ang terminong \"entangled\":\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|00\\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"and this state is called a **Bell state**.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|00\\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"at ang estadong ito ay tinatawag na **Bell state**.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An entangled state is a state $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ consisting of quantum states $|\\psi_A\\rangle$ and $|\\psi_B\\rangle$ that cannot be represented by a tensor product of individual quantum states.\n"
msgstr "Ang entangled state ay isang estado na $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ na binubuo ng mga quantum state na $|\\psi_A\\rangle$ at $|\\psi_B\\rangle$ na hindi maaaring katawanin bilang tensor product ng mga indibidwal na quantum state.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ below has two states $|\\psi\\rangle_A$ and $|\\psi\\rangle_B$;\n"
msgstr "Kung ang $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ sa ibaba ay may dalawang estado na $|\\psi\\rangle_A$ at $|\\psi\\rangle_B$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle +|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle_A|0\\rangle_B +|1\\rangle_A|1\\rangle_B)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle +|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle_A|0\\rangle_B +|1\\rangle_A|1\\rangle_B)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_A = a_0|0\\rangle+a_1|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_B = b_0|0\\rangle+b_1|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_A = a_0|0\\rangle+a_1|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_B = b_0|0\\rangle+b_1|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "the tensor product of these two states is the following\n"
msgstr "ang tensor product ng dalawang estadong ito ay ang sumusunod\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle _A\\otimes |\\psi\\rangle _B = a_0 b_0|00\\rangle+a_0 b_1|01\\rangle+a_1 b_0|10\\rangle+a_1 b_1|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle _A\\otimes |\\psi\\rangle _B = a_0 b_0|00\\rangle+a_0 b_1|01\\rangle+a_1 b_0|10\\rangle+a_1 b_1|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "but there are no coefficients $a_0, a_1, b_0, $ and $b_1$ to satisfy these two equations. Therefore, $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ is not represented by a tensor product of individual quantum state, $|\\psi\\rangle_A$ and $|\\psi\\rangle_B$, and this means that $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle +|11\\rangle)$ is entangled state.\n"
msgstr "ngunit walang mga coefficient na $a_0, a_1, b_0,$ at $b_1$ na makakatugon sa dalawang equation na ito. Samakatuwid, ang $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ ay hindi maaaring katawanin bilang tensor product ng mga indibidwal na quantum state na $|\\psi\\rangle_A$ at $|\\psi\\rangle_B$, at nangangahulugan ito na ang $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle +|11\\rangle)$ ay isang entangled state.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us create the Bell state and run it on a real quantum computer. Now we will follow the four steps to writing a quantum program, called **Qiskit patterns**:\n"
msgstr "Gawin natin ang Bell state at patakbuhin ito sa isang tunay na quantum computer. Susundin natin ang apat na hakbang sa pagsulat ng quantum program, na tinatawag na **Qiskit patterns**:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map problem to quantum circuits and operators\n"
msgstr "I-map ang problema sa mga quantum circuit at operator\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize for target hardware\n"
msgstr "I-optimize para sa target na hardware\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute on target hardware\n"
msgstr "Isabuhay sa target na hardware\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process the results\n"
msgstr "I-post-process ang mga resulta\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1. Map problem to quantum circuits and operators {#step-1-map-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1. I-map ang problema sa mga quantum circuit at operator {#step-1-map-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a quantum program, quantum circuits are the native format in which to represent quantum instructions. When creating a circuit, you'll usually create a new QuantumCircuit object, then add instructions to it in sequence.\n"
msgstr "Sa isang quantum program, ang mga quantum circuit ang katutubong format para katawanin ang mga quantum instruction. Kapag gumagawa ng circuit, kadalasan ay gagawa ka ng bagong QuantumCircuit object, tapos magdadagdag ng mga instruction nang sunod-sunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code cell creates a circuit that produces a Bell state, the specific two-qubit entangled state from above.\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod na code cell ay gumagawa ng circuit na nagpo-produce ng Bell state — ang partikular na two-qubit entangled state mula sa itaas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/5fdd9317-8fab-46ee-ac6d-25ef031dd52b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/5fdd9317-8fab-46ee-ac6d-25ef031dd52b-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2. Optimize for target hardware {#step-2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2. I-optimize para sa target na hardware {#step-2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "Qiskit converts abstract circuits to QISA (Quantum Instruction Set Architecture) circuits that respect the constraints of the target hardware and optimizes circuit performance. So before the optimization, we will specify the target hardware.\n"
#| "If you do not have `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, you will need to install this first. For more information about Qiskit Runtime, [check out the API reference.](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/runtime-service)\n"
msgid ""
"Qiskit converts abstract circuits to QISA (Quantum Instruction Set Architecture) circuits that respect the constraints of the target hardware and optimizes circuit performance. So before the optimization, we will specify the target hardware.\n"
"If you do not have `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, you will need to install this first. For more information, [check out the API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/runtime-service).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kino-convert ng Qiskit ang mga abstract circuit sa QISA (Quantum Instruction Set Architecture) circuit na sumusunod sa mga limitasyon ng target na hardware at ino-optimize ang circuit performance. Kaya bago ang optimization, tutukuyin muna natin ang target na hardware.\n"
"Kung wala kang `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, kailangan mo itong i-install muna. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa Qiskit Runtime, [tingnan ang API reference.](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/runtime-service)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will specify the target hardware.\n"
msgstr "Tutukuyin natin ang target na hardware.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpiling the circuit is yet another complex process. Very briefly, this rewrites the circuit into a logically equivalent one using \"native gates\" (gates that a particular quantum computer can implement) and maps the qubits in your circuit to optimal real qubits on the target quantum computer. For more on transpilation, see this [documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/transpiler#overview).\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-transpile ng circuit ay isang kumplikadong proseso. Sa madaling salita, sine-rewrite nito ang circuit sa isang logically equivalent na bersyon gamit ang \"native gates\" (mga gate na kaya ng isang partikular na quantum computer na isagawa) at imi-map ang mga qubit sa iyong circuit sa pinakamainam na tunay na mga qubit sa target na quantum computer. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa transpilation, tingnan ang [dokumentasyong ito](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/transpiler#overview).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can see that in the transpilation the circuit was rewritten using new gates. For more information, refer to the [ECRGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.ECRGate#ecrgate) documentation.\n"
msgstr "Makikita mo na sa transpilation ay na-rewrite ang circuit gamit ang mga bagong gate. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon, tingnan ang dokumentasyon ng [ECRGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.ECRGate#ecrgate).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3. Execute the target circuit {#step-3-execute-the-target-circuit}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3. Isabuhay ang target circuit {#step-3-execute-the-target-circuit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, we will run the target circuit on the real device.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, patakbuhin natin ang target circuit sa tunay na device.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution on the real device might require waiting in a queue, since quantum computers are valuable resources, and very much in demand. The job_id is used to check the execution status and results of the job later.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpapatakbo sa tunay na device ay maaaring mangailangan ng paghihintay sa pila, dahil ang mga quantum computer ay mahahalagang mapagkukunan at lubos na hinahangad. Ang job_id ay ginagamit para suriin ang katayuan ng pagpapatakbo at mga resulta ng trabaho sa bandang huli.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
